#0 indicates previous year values

####Two figures
####Sliding window analysis to test the stepwise changes in direction (positive or negative) and strength (adj. R2) of the linear relationship between the mean weight of age-1 of the GoR spring spawning herring and: a, b) spawning stock biomass (SSB, thousand tons); c, d) abundance of E. affinis affinis in May (copepodite stages I–III; ln(ind. m-2))); e, f) abundance of E. affinis affinis in August (copepod nauplii; ln(ind. m-2))). Left panels: slopes of the linear model (points) and mean value of the respective explanatory variable (grey line), fitted to each 15-year subset of data. Error bars show the standard error of the slope for subsets where the slope was significant at p <0.05. Right panels: adjusted R2 of the linear model fitted in every step. Filled points show where the model was significant at p <0.05.,
####Sliding window analysis to test the stepwise change in the direction (positive or negative) and strength (adj. R2) of the linear relationship between the mean weight of age-1 of the GoR spring spawning herring and: a, b) abundance of Acartia spp. (adult copepods, ln(ind. m-2)) in May; c, d) abundance of E. affinis affinis and Acartia spp. (copepodite stages IV–V, ln(ind. m-2)) in August; e, f) abundance of E. affinis affinis and Acartia spp. (adult copepods, ln(ind. m-2)) in May. Left panel: slopes of the linear model (points) and mean value of the respective explanatory variable (grey line), fitted to each 15-year subset of data. Error bars show the standard error of the slope for subsets where the slope was significant at p <0.05. Right panels: adjusted R2 of the linear model fitted in every step. Filled points show where the model was significant at p <0.05.

